Mocha LLM
Original integration and MiniMind CPU/CUDA inference code: Pisces-Moze and contributors, 2026.

Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct weights, tokenizer and model architecture:
Qwen / Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0; see licenses/Qwen-Apache-2.0.txt.
Q8 conversion and standalone inference implementation are modifications by this project.

Optional Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct GGUF weights: Qwen / Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0.
Optional Llama 3.2 1B Instruct GGUF weights: Meta, Llama 3.2 Community License
and Acceptable Use Policy, not MIT or Apache-2.0. Built with Llama.
The Llama quantization is distributed by bartowski; fixed revisions/hashes are
in models/large-models.json. Weights are downloaded separately, not stored in Git.
See licenses/Llama-3.2-LICENSE.txt and licenses/Llama-3.2-USE-POLICY.md.
The ARMv7 CPU GGUF engine is llama.cpp b4514, MIT, from the ggml authors.
See licenses/llama.cpp-MIT.txt. CPU mode does not use the Mocha CUDA runtime;
the optional native GGUF quantized matmul bridge uses the application-private runtime.
The bridge's quantized block interpretation follows ggml (MIT).
AirLLM (Apache-2.0) is a design reference for bounded streaming, not a bundled
framework or copied implementation; its PyTorch stack is not installed by this tool.

MiniMind2-Small development reference tokenizer and model architecture:
jingyaogong / MiniMind, Apache-2.0; see licenses/MiniMind-Apache-2.0.txt.
Q8 conversion and standalone inference implementation are modifications by this project.
The model's pinned README declares Apache-2.0 in its License section.

TinyStories 260K weights and tokenizer: karpathy/tinyllamas (MIT).
TinyStories host engine: Andrej Karpathy / llama2.c (MIT), modified to add CUDA forward,
optional CPU comparisons and diagnostics. See licenses/llama2.c-MIT.txt.

Application-local runtime: Shinpei Kato and other Gdev contributors (MIT), with Mocha patches.
Includes the upstream Ocelot/Hydrazine code and author notices from Gdev's pinned source.
See licenses/Gdev-MIT.txt and runtime-source/sources.json.
Private libdrm / libdrm_nouveau and Boost.Thread retain their distribution copyright
and license notices under licenses/. System glibc, libstdc++, libgcc and libgomp
are dependencies and are not bundled.

NVIDIA's CUDA toolkit, compiler, headers and proprietary runtime are NOT shipped.
The application contains its own CUDA kernels compiled to native sm_32 code.
This is an experimental open runtime port, not NVIDIA's complete CUDA distribution.
